  "summary": [
    "Pace through February 2026 (~606 deaths) combined with historical annual tolls around 2,100–2,500 makes reaching 1,000 deaths by May 2026 plausible.",
    "Seasonal factors and weather could elevate crossing risk in spring, supporting a higher likelihood, while SAR policy changes could dampen fatalities.",
    "Calibrated posterior reflects strong early-year data but acknowledges reporting lags and year-to-year variability."
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "narrative": "Early-year death counts plus high historical baselines suggest a non-negligible chance of surpassing 1,000 Mediterranean deaths by May 2026. The posterior probability is calibrated at 0.94, with a range that accommodates ongoing pace, seasonal dynamics, and uncertainties in reporting and policy effects.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.75,
      "basis": "reference class anchored to central Mediterranean annual death tolls and the observed pace through February 2026; chosen as a neutral starting point before updates from March–April."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Ongoing pace through March–April 2026",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "606 deaths by end of February 2026; continuation at a similar pace into March–April would push totals toward or beyond 1,000 by May."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Historical base-rate for Mediterranean deaths (2,100–2,500 per year range in recent years)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Strong baseline mortality supports plausibility of reaching 1,000 by May if current pace persists."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Weather and sea conditions increasing crossing risk (seasonal factors in spring)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Spring conditions often yield more crossings and higher mortality risk."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Search-and-rescue capacity and policy environment",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Improved SAR or stricter controls could reduce fatalities, dampening the probability of hitting 1,000 by May."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Data verification lag and undercount risk",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Delayed verifications could add to counts, nudging totals upward toward the threshold."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Primary drivers are the current pace and the historical base-rate, which collectively raise the probability toward 1,000 by May. Moderating factors (policy/SAR dynamics) dampen the estimate, while data-lag risks could push counts higher. The final posterior (0.94) reflects these competing updates, with a calibrated uncertainty range that accounts for potential revisions and seasonal variability."
  }
}

